# Slice 289 (INDEX-NUMERIC-RECEPTION): this program has no receiver of the conversion of an int into size_t, so an int index of
# the L3 INDEX of a machine pointer an own field holds is refused by the ordinary numeric reception, as any reception of an
# int into size_t is -- never an unchecked C index. CHECK admits the reception in the program's order: the next line's
# refusal does not come first.
[]: int cells 2
cells[1U]: 7
@: pc int @ cells[0U]
int: at 1
int: got pc[at]
int: later "text"
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
